    }
    return day;
}


Switch Statements Since Java 12
Since the new Java 12 features, the same code can be simplified as follows:

public static String getDayOfWeek(int dayNum) {
    return switch (dayNum) {
        case 1 -> "Monday";
        case 2 -> "Tuesday";
        case 3 -> "Wednesday";
        case 4 -> "Thursday";
        case 5 -> "Friday";
        case 6 -> "Saturday";
        case 7 -> "Sunday";
        default -> "Invalid day";
    };
}
As shown in the example, since Java 12, the case statements now use the new arrow operator (->) to 
specify the pattern and the result expression. It also eliminates the break statement at each case.

